,"message":"Add Jira fingerprinting system for skill execution tracking\n\nImplements comprehensive fingerprinting to track Quality Tiger Team skill\nexecutions in Jira for team-tracker dashboard consumption.\n\nFeatures:\n- One tracking issue per repository (RHOAIENG project)\n- Label-based fingerprinting (skill-name-executed, status labels)\n- Detailed execution comments (timestamp, results, artifacts)\n- Works locally (Jira API) and ready for Ambient (MCP)\n- Graceful degradation when Jira not configured\n- Reuses existing tracking issues (no duplicates)\n\nImplementation:\n- fingerprint_utils.py: Core fingerprinting logic\n  - record_skill_execution(): Main entry point\n  - find_or_create_tracking_issue(): Issue management\n  - generate_execution_comment(): Comment formatting\n- jira_utils.py: Jira API integration (from RFE creator)\n  - API calls with Basic Auth\n  - Issue creation/update\n  - Label management\n  - ADF conversion (markdown to Atlassian Document Format)\n\nTested:\n- End-to-end with redhat.atlassian.net\n- All 3 skills (quality-repo-analysis, konflux-build-simulator, test-rules-generator)\n- Issue reuse verified (RHOAIENG-56528)\n- Labels accumulating correctly\n- Comments posting with full details\n\nFixes:\n- JQL search endpoint (updated to /rest/api/3/search/jql for HTTP 410 fix)\n- Priority field handling (made optional)\n- URL encoding (switched to POST body)\n\nDocumentation:\n- FINGERPRINTING-DESIGN.md: Complete design and options\n- FINGERPRINTING-IMPLEMENTATION.md: Usage guide and setup\n- FINGERPRINTING-TEST-RESULTS.md: Test results and next steps\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6efda7b917029db3789d5885200ac7aa2ed0deff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/antowaddle/Red-Hat-Quality-Tiger-Team/git/trees/6efda7b917029db3789d5885200ac7aa2ed0deff"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/antowaddle/Red-Hat-Quality-Tiger-Team/git/commits/c2633eb9255803dab4581341c0c0005900f36147","verification":{"payl