mail.com","name":"Mitch Avis"},"message":"docs(shell-scripting): scale the workflow and drop the default ifs\n\nEvery shell task, including a Makefile recipe or a CI step, ran the full production workflow\n(intent interview, template, dry-run flags, Bats tests). There is now a light path (strict mode,\nquoting, ShellCheck) and a full path for production scripts. IFS=$''\\n\\t'' leaves the default header:\nit silently broke read splitting, needed a warning to explain, and quoting already makes\niteration safe; scope IFS to the command that needs it instead.","tree":{"sha":"2de708b49076565590d2b5b81a30a54fde6171be","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitch-avis/agent-skills/git/trees/2de708b49076565590d2b5b81a30a54fde6171be"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitch-avis/agent-skills/git/commits/2f5956bb76d280f3462e49a5acec8c70f4a91810","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/111894662?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mitch-avis","id":111894662,"login":"mitch-avis","node_id":"U_kgDOBqtghg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mitch-avis/agent-skills/commit/2f5956bb76d280f3462e49a5acec8c70f4a91810","node_id":"C_kwDOR1JTGtoAKDJmNTk1NmJiNzZkMjgwZjM0NjJlNDlhNWFjZWM4YzcwZjRhOTE4MTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mitch-avis/agent-skills/commit/6a39feed5d3260505cc47c3e436897421f89e0cb","sha":"6a39feed5d3260505cc47c3e436897421f89e0cb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitch-avis/agent-skills/commits/6a39feed5d3260505cc47c3e436897421f89e0cb"}],"sha":"2f5956bb76d280f3462e49a5acec8c70f4a91810","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitch-avis/agent-skills/commits/2f5956bb76d280f3462e49a5acec8c70f4a91810"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/111894662?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mitch-avis","id":111894662,"login":"mitch-avis","node_id":"U_kgDOBqtghg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitch-avis/agent-skills/commits/6a39feed5d3260505cc47c3e436897421f89e0cb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T08:34:03Z","email":"mitchavis@gmail.com","name":"Mitch Avis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T08:34:03Z","email":"mitchavis@gmail.com","name":"Mitch Avis"},"message":"docs(observability): scope service-grade telemetry to services\n\nThe task rule routes any logging change to this skill, and its checklist demanded OTel traces,\nRED/USE metrics, dashboards, and SLO alerts, so a literal agent could wire Prometheus into a CLI\nto add a log line. A scope section now separates CLIs, scripts, and batch jobs (structured logs,\nlevels, no secrets) from long-running services, and the checklist is labeled for services. Also\nmarks correlation.id as app-defined; it is not an ECS field.","tree":{"sha":"d35822914edc73ff991dba1adace8106264a016c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitch-avis/agent-skills/git/trees/d35822914edc73ff991dba1adace8106264a016c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitch-avis/agent-skills/git/commits/6a39feed5d3260505cc47c3e436897421f89e0cb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/111894662?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mitch-avis","id":111894662,"login":"mitch-avis","node_id":"U_kgDOBqtghg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mitch-avis/agent-skills/commit/6a39feed5d3260505cc47c3e436897421f89e0cb","node_id":"C_kwDOR1JTGtoAKDZhMzlmZWVkNWQzMjYwNTA1Y2M0N2MzZTQzNjg5NzQyMWY4OWUwY2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mitch-avis/agent-skills/commit/0b666390b8f488925ce9bc69f25f7e124dc9927d","sha":"0b666390b8f488925ce9bc69f25f7e124dc9927d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitch-avis/agent-skills/commits/0b666390b8f488925ce9bc69f25f7e124dc9927d"}],"sha":"6a39feed5d3260505cc47c3e436897421f89e0cb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitch-avis/agent-skills/commits/6a39feed5d3260505cc47c3e436897421f89e0cb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/111894662?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mitch-avis","id":111894662,"login":"mitch-avis","node_id":"U_kgDOBqtghg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitch-avis/agent-skills/commits/0b666390b8f488925ce9bc69f25f7e124dc9927d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T08:33:52Z","email":"mitchavis@gmail.com","name":"Mitch Avis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T08:33:52Z","email":"mitchavis@gmail.com","name":"Mitch Avis"},"message":"test: adopt arrange-act-assert structure in checker tests\n\nStructure and labels only; no behavior change. Assertions that wrapped the call now assign\nthe result in the Act phase.","tree":{"sha":"e4e018ef50e083d59746e337fedfad2e3f17be57","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitch-avis/agent-skills/git/trees/e4e018ef50e083d59746e337fedfad2e3f17be57"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitch-avis/agent-skills/git/commits/0b666390b8f488925ce9bc69f25f7e124dc9927d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/111894662?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mitch-avis","id":111894662,"login":"mitch-avis","node_id":"U_kgDOBqtghg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mitch-avis/agent-skills/commit/0b666390b8f488925ce9bc69f25f7e124dc9927d","node_id":"C_kwDOR1JTGtoAKDBiNjY2MzkwYjhmNDg4OTI1Y2U5YmM2OWYyNWY3ZTEyNGRjOTkyN2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mitch-avis/agent-skills/commit/a8da2c992d80ecd1bbf9a655b138601e57d1bd27","sha":"a8da2c992d80ecd1bbf9a655b138601e57d1bd27","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitch-avis/agent-skills/commits/a8da2c992d80ecd1bbf9a655b138601e57d1bd27"}],"sha":"0b666390b8f488925ce9bc69f25f7e124dc9927d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitch-avis/agent-skills/commits/0b666390b8f488925ce9bc69f25f7e124dc9927d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/111894662?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mitch-avis","id":111894662,"login":"mitch-avis","node_id":"U_kgDOBqtghg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitch-avis/agent-skills/commits/a8da2c992d80ecd1bbf9a655b138601e57d1bd27/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T08:33:28Z","email":"mitchavis@gmail.com","name":"Mitch Avis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T08:33:28Z","email":"mitchavis@gmail.com","name":"Mitch Avis"},"message":"docs: require arrange-act-assert with labeled phases in all tests\n\nThe test-driven-development skill now defines the house test structure: labeled # Arrange,\n# Act, and # Assert phases separated by blank lines, one action per test, # Act & Assert for\nraises/should_panic/toThrow, and no Arrange when there is no setup. Before editing a test file\nthat predates the rule, agents convert the whole file in its own test: commit.\n\npython-testing, rust-testing, and frontend-react point to the rule, every test example in the\nskills follows it, and code-review and python-anti-patterns check for it. Along the way, async\ntest examples use fakes instead of live URLs, and the TypeScript anti-pattern examples gain the\nmissing async and the assertion they described but never made.","tree":{"sha":"a5143434a317e5aac1fb2003da1c01e67dcce920","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitch-avis/agent-skills/git/trees/a5143434a317e5aac1fb2003da1c01e67dcce920"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitch-avis/agent-skills/git/commits/a8da2c992d80ecd1bbf9a655b138601e57d1bd27","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/111894662?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mitch-avis","id":111894662,"login":"mitch-avis","node_id":"U_kgDOBqtghg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mitch-avis/agent-skills/commit/a8da2c992d80ecd1bbf9a655b138601e57d1bd27","node_id":"C_kwDOR1JTGtoAKGE4ZGEyYzk5MmQ4MGVjZDFiYmY5YTY1NWIxMzg2MDFlNTdkMWJkMjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mitch-avis/agent-skills/commit/9134e236dcf5405ebca04b0fe271f6503eb9952b","sha":"9134e236dcf5405ebca04b0fe271f6503eb9952b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitch-avis/agent-skills/commits/9134e236dcf5405ebca04b0fe271f6503eb9952b"}],"sha":"a8da2c992d80ecd1bbf9a655b138601e57d1bd27","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitch-avis/agent-skills/commits/a8da2c992d80ecd1bbf9a655b138601e57d1bd27"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/111894662?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mitch-avis","id":111894662,"login":"mitch-avis","node_id":"U_kgDOBqtghg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitch-avis/agent-skills/commits/9134e236dcf5405ebca04b0fe271f6503eb9952b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T08:31:51Z","email":"mitchavis@gmail.com","name":"Mitch Avis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T08:31:51Z","email":"mitchavis@gmail.com","name":"Mitch Avis"},"message":"docs(systematic-debugging): write the rules at normal volume\n\nAll-caps emphasis on a dozen lines (ALWAYS, ANY, BEFORE, STOP, MUST, FASTER) made every rule\nlook equally urgent, which invites over-application such as running all four phases for a\ntypo. Same rules, normal case. The routing description and the Iron Law block are unchanged.","tree":{"sha":"4b358b79c58b0617bdcec82ffd1cd312c7db5d4b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitch-avis/agent-skills/git/trees/4b358b79c58b0617bdcec82ffd1cd312c7db5d4b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitch-avis/agent-skills/git/commits/9134e236dcf5405ebca04b0fe271f6503eb9952b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/111894662?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mitch-avis","id":111894662,"login":"mitch-avis","node_id":"U_kgDOBqtghg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mitch-avis/agent-skills/commit/9134e236dcf5405ebca04b0fe271f6503eb9952b","node_id":"C_kwDOR1JTGtoAKDkxMzRlMjM2ZGNmNTQwNWViY2EwNGIwZmUyNzFmNjUwM2ViOTk1MmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mitch-avis/agent-skills/commit/3f59631e0f60bf0ef93b668a9a15805466ffbbde","sha":"3f59631e0f60bf0ef93b668a9a15805466ffbbde","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitch-avis/agent-skills/commits/3f59631e0f60bf0ef93b668a9a15805466ffbbde"}],"sha":"9134e236dcf5405ebca04b0fe271f6503eb9952b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitch-avis/agent-skills/commits/9134e236dcf5405ebca04b0fe271f6503eb9952b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/111894662?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mitch-avis","id":111894662,"login":"mitch-avis","node_id":"U_kgDOBqtghg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mitch-avis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitch-avis/agent-skills/commits/3f59631e0f60bf0ef93b668a9a15805466ffbbde/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T08:31:34Z","email":"mitchavis@gmail.com","name":"Mitch Avis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T08:31:34Z","email":"mitchavis@gmail.com","name":"Mitch Avis"},"message":"docs(test-driven-development): keep the rules, drop the pressure wording\n\nCurrent models follow text literally, so ''delete it, start over, delete means delete'',\nMANDATORY banners, and a Final Rule restating the Iron Law could make an agent discard working\ncode. The rules stay (test first, watch it fail, small fixes exempt); the remedy is now ''go back\nto RED'' or ''re-implement from the failing test''. Examples move from TypeScript and npm to pytest\nwith a Rust note, the checklist asks for a test per behavior rather than per function, the\nrationalization table keeps the five rows not stated elsewhere, the anti-pattern Iron Laws\nbecome rules with reasons, and the mermaid labels use <br> so line breaks render.","tree":{"sha":"4e6bf8278db78fd11a5e03e5c3e285b21aec5542","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitch-avis/agent-skills/git/trees/4e6bf8278db78fd11a5e03e5c3e285b21aec5542"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitch-avis/agent-skills/git/commits/3f59631e0f60bf0ef93b668a9a15805466ffbbde","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https:/