i.github.com/users/cchifor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/commits/2f43dc6a782cfff2765b5e8764c36425657be179/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-17T20:37:36Z","email":"chifor@gmail.com","name":"Catalin Chifor"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-17T20:37:36Z","email":"chifor@gmail.com","name":"Catalin Chifor"},"message":"fix(auth): node/rust permissive trust-map default\n\nThe Node and Rust platform-auth SDK AuthGuards ran _enforceTrust whenever\na trust map was present and unconditionally rejected a token whose tenant\nhad no record (`unknown tenant`). bootstrapAuth/init_auth always install\nan empty InMemoryIssuerTrustMap, so every authenticated request to a\ndefault-generated Node/Rust backend 401''d — the auth subsystem was unusable\nout of the box for two of three backend languages.\n\nMirror Python''s AuthGuard(strict_trust=False) default: a missing trust\nrecord is accepted (the permissive single-issuer default); per-tenant\nissuer binding + suspension only constrain explicitly-registered tenants.\nAdd a strictTrust/strict_trust opt-in (default false) for hybrid-realm\ndeployments, raising IssuerNotTrusted to match Python.\n\nAdds cross-SDK parity scenario accept_unregistered_tenant_when_trust_map_present\n(red on Node+Rust before the fix, green after; Python already permissive).","tree":{"sha":"a592df9340684a33a4ccdd47b59cb7098ee38b35","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/git/trees/a592df9340684a33a4ccdd47b59cb7098ee38b35"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/git/commits/2f43dc6a782cfff2765b5e8764c36425657be179","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13657847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cchifor","id":13657847,"login":"cchifor","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNjU3ODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cchifor/forge/commit/2f43dc6a782cfff2765b5e8764c36425657be179","node_id":"C_kwDOR12LHtoAKDJmNDNkYzZhNzgyY2ZmZjI3NjViNWU4NzY0YzM2NDI1NjU3YmUxNzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cchifor/forge/commit/1acc005155519a626b18c84ed0cada0ccec70088","sha":"1acc005155519a626b18c84ed0cada0ccec70088","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/commits/1acc005155519a626b18c84ed0cada0ccec70088"}],"sha":"2f43dc6a782cfff2765b5e8764c36425657be179","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/commits/2f43dc6a782cfff2765b5e8764c36425657be179"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13657847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cchifor","id":13657847,"login":"cchifor","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNjU3ODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/commits/1acc005155519a626b18c84ed0cada0ccec70088/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-17T18:38:59Z","email":"chifor@gmail.com","name":"Constantin Chifor"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-17T18:38:59Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: node/rust auth-path generate + no-auth CRUD bugs (#281)\n\nTwo generator bugs found during e2e validation:\n- node+Keycloak `forge generate` aborted (npm enoent) — per-backend toolchain install ran before the project-scoped platform-auth-node SDK + workspace-root package.json existed; deferred install past _apply_project_scope.\n- node/rust no-auth (auth.mode=none) CRUD endpoints 500''d on an unbound request identity; ship a dev-identity binder wired only when auth is off, mirroring Python''s dev passthrough.\n\nAlso: the smoke contract now exercises the CRUD path so data-path 500s can''t slip through a health+OpenAPI-only check.","tree":{"sha":"33033038b94a094f7584d70a144f06734d8b06f0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/git/trees/33033038b94a094f7584d70a144f06734d8b06f0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/git/commits/1acc005155519a626b18c84ed0cada0ccec70088","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cchifor/forge/commit/1acc005155519a626b18c84ed0cada0ccec70088","node_id":"C_kwDOR12LHtoAKDFhY2MwMDUxNTU1MTlhNjI2YjE4Yzg0ZWQwY2FkYTBjY2VjNzAwODg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cchifor/forge/commit/243ed105aa80a5db8a1aa284c9736837fe3ad7ac","sha":"243ed105aa80a5db8a1aa284c9736837fe3ad7ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/commits/243ed105aa80a5db8a1aa284c9736837fe3ad7ac"}],"sha":"1acc005155519a626b18c84ed0cada0ccec70088","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/commits/1acc005155519a626b18c84ed0cada0ccec70088"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13657847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cchifor","id":13657847,"login":"cchifor","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNjU3ODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/commits/243ed105aa80a5db8a1aa284c9736837fe3ad7ac/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-17T10:13:49Z","email":"chifor@gmail.com","name":"Constantin Chifor"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-17T10:13:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: sync docs with landed #258/#260 work (#280)\n\nReflect the merged changes in the docs that drifted (audit was workflow-\ndriven + adversarially verified):\n\n- CHANGELOG [Unreleased]: entries for #274 (stateless update fix), #275\n  (cache-scope, preset fuzzer, nightly scenario naming, doc-truth gate),\n  #276 (OPERATIONS/OBSERVABILITY runbooks), #278 (flutter bearer), #279\n  (rust OTLP otel).\n- docs/known-issues.md: drop the ''observability.otel is a stub on Rust''\n  row — #279 shipped the real OTLP impl.\n- observability.otel option description -> python/node/rust; regen\n  docs/FEATURES.md via tools/gen_features_doc.py (FEATURES.md is generated).\n- rust OBSERVABILITY.md: correct the unset-endpoint behaviour (no OTLP\n  layer registered; structured logs still emit). Golden snapshot regen.\n- docs/architecture.md + docs/rfcs/RFC-002: fix ''forge migrate --only'' /\n  ''forge --migrate-only'' to the real ''forge --migrate --migrate-only''\n  (same drift class the doc-truth gate now guards in user-facing docs).\n\nRefs #258 #260","tree":{"sha":"ff067a2a556e8017b6e8c1fe6af1ebfa87a080cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/git/trees/ff067a2a556e8017b6e8c1fe6af1ebfa87a080cd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/git/comm