:{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cchifor/forge/commit/8ee8297aec40aa2895976fbeaf31b5b172a84f04","node_id":"C_kwDOR12LHtoAKDhlZTgyOTdhZWM0MGFhMjg5NTk3NmZiZWFmMzFiNWIxNzJhODRmMDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cchifor/forge/commit/6526e58397f66cd537f3b4b8050a90f472f83fa3","sha":"6526e58397f66cd537f3b4b8050a90f472f83fa3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/commits/6526e58397f66cd537f3b4b8050a90f472f83fa3"}],"sha":"8ee8297aec40aa2895976fbeaf31b5b172a84f04","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/commits/8ee8297aec40aa2895976fbeaf31b5b172a84f04"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13657847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cchifor","id":13657847,"login":"cchifor","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNjU3ODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/commits/6526e58397f66cd537f3b4b8050a90f472f83fa3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-16T13:30:34Z","email":"chifor@gmail.com","name":"Constantin Chifor"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-16T13:30:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: #264 follow-ups + JWKS_URI gatekeeper auth fix (#265)\n\n* fix(auth): point backend server_url + audience at gatekeeper\n\nIn the gatekeeper sole-issuer model the backend validates gatekeeper''s\ninternal ES256 JWT (iss=gatekeeper:5000, JWKS at <server_url>/auth/jwks,\naud=forge-services for both ForwardAuth and S2S tokens). Compose+helm set\nSERVER_URL=keycloak:8080 and never set the expected audience, so a real\nkeycloak backend (dev_mode off) would reject every gatekeeper token. Point\nserver_url at gatekeeper and set APP__SECURITY__AUTH__AUDIENCE=forge-services.\nThe S2S e2e now also hits a protected route (401 without a token, 200 with)\nso this can''t regress unnoticed.\n\n* fix(webhooks): reject DNS names that resolve to private IPs\n\nNode and Rust webhook delivery validated only literal hosts; a hostname\nresolving to a loopback/RFC1918/link-local/metadata IP slipped through.\nResolve the host (dns.lookup / to_socket_addrs) and reject any internal\nresolved address, matching Python''s connect-time guard.\n\n* fix(oidc): seed trust map + enable strict_trust for oidc_generic\n\noidc_generic relied on the SDK guard''s permissive missing-record default.\nSeed the trust map with the configured issuer and pass strict_trust=True so\nthe configured issuer is accepted while unknown issuers fail closed.\n\n* fix(rate-limit): only trust X-Forwarded-For behind a private peer\n\nKeying on the left-most XFF unconditionally lets a directly-exposed app be\nspoofed. Honor XFF only when the transport peer is a private/loopback address\n(behind an in-cluster proxy); otherwise key on the peer (py + rust).\n\n* fix: helm registry list shape, rust S2S i64, layout validation\n\n- Helm gatekeeper registry placeholder renders services: [] (a list, per the\n  ServiceRegistry schema) not services: {}.\n- Rust S2S expires_in is Option<i64> so a negative value coerces to 300\n  instead of failing deserialization.\n- FrontendConfig.validate rejects an explicitly-unsupported layout even when\n  the framework has no supported variants.\n\n* test(golden): refresh snapshots for auth-config + rate-limit fixes\n\n* test: pin backend->gatekeeper auth config (structural guard)\n\nThe full-stack S2S e2e revealed a deeper, separate bug: even with the correct\nserver_url/audience, the backend''s JWKS cache fails to fetch gatekeeper''s\nJWKS at runtime (httpx _fetch raises while the endpoint is reachable via\nurllib from the same container) -> tokens are rejected. That is tracked\nseparately. Drop the (currently-blocked) protected-route assertion from the\ne2e and instead pin the server_url/audience invariant structurally:\nAPP__SECURITY__AUTH__SERVER_URL == GATEKEEPER_ISSUER (gatekeeper) and\nAUDIENCE == the gatekeeper INTERNAL_TOKEN_AUDIENCE.\n\n* test: make cache_port app stub augmenting (xdist-safe)\n\nUnder pytest -n auto a sibling on the same worker can insert a bare\n`app` package (e.g. the oidc trust-map test) before this one runs. The\nold skip-if-present guard (`if \"app\" not in sys.modules`) then left\n`app.ports` unstubbed -> ModuleNotFoundError. Backfill each of app /\napp.ports / app.ports.cache individually so the stub is order-independent.\n\n* fix(auth): pin backend JWKS_URI to gatekeeper endpoint\n\nPointing server_url at gatekeeper was necessary but not sufficient:\nforge_core''s auth setup derives the JWKS URI from server_url + realm as\nthe Keycloak-style /realms/<realm>/protocol/openid-connect/certs path\nunless APP__SECURITY__AUTH__JWKS_URI is set. Gatekeeper does not serve\nthat path (its JWKS is at /auth/jwks), so the backend 404''d on every\nverification and rejected every gatekeeper token with ''JWKS unavailable\n... stale window expired''.\n\nPin JWKS_URI to http://gatekeeper:5000/auth/jwks in the keycloak compose\nand Helm backend env. Proven end-to-end: the headless-api boot now hits\na *protected* route (/api/v1/items) — rejecting a malformed bearer (401)\nand accepting a freshly-minted gatekeeper token (200). The prior e2e only\nhit /api/v1/health/live, which AuthContextMiddleware excludes from\nverification, so it never exercised the verifier.","tree":{"sha":"4d56293f8cf6d5960fa6bc421adb2f5e68ac89fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/git/trees/4d56293f8cf6d5960fa6bc421adb2f5e68ac89fd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/git/commits/6526e58397f66cd537f3b4b8050a90f472f83fa3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cchifor/forge/commit/6526e58397f66cd537f3b4b8050a90f472f83fa3","node_id":"C_kwDOR12LHtoAKDY1MjZlNTgzOTdmNjZjZDUzN2YzYjRiODA1MGE5MGY0NzJmODNmYTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cchifor/forge/commit/b648413f7b6a62930f96efa819090d15cabe5caa","sha":"b648413f7b6a62930f96efa819090d15cabe5caa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/commits/b648413f7b6a62930f96efa819090d15cabe5caa"}],"sha":"6526e58397f66cd537f3b4b8050a90f472f83fa3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/commits/6526e58397f66cd537f3b4b8050a90f472f83fa3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13657847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cchifor","id":13657847,"login":"cchifor","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNjU3ODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/commits/b648413f7b6a62930f96efa819090d15cabe5caa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-16T09:51:22Z","email":"chifor@gmail.com","name":"Constantin Chifor"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-16T09:51:22Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: triaged second-audit remediation (27 bugs) (#263)\n\n* fix(auth): oidc trust-map default, HSTS + rate-limit behind proxy\n\n- platform-auth SDK AuthGuard: a missing trust record is now permissive by\n  default (new strict_trust=True opt-in restores fail-closed). The oidc_generic\n  provider builds an EMPTY InMemoryIssuerTrustMap, so the old unconditional\n  fail-closed path 401''d every valid token — the provider authenticated nobody.\n- security-headers (py+rust): honor x-forwarded-proto so HSTS is emitted behind\n  a TLS-terminating proxy (the documented Traefik deploy), not just on direct https.\n- rate-limit (py+rust): derive the client key from X-Forwarded-For so clients\n  behind a proxy get independent budgets, and bound/evict idle buckets (LRU).\n\n* fix(domain): spec loader, pydantic defaults, Dart extras round-trip\n\n- spec loader: entity YAML without an indices block no longer crashes\n  (or () -> or []), and min/max_length are int>=0 validated.\n- pydantic emitter renders EntityField.default (defaulted fields were emitted\n  as required, diverging from the SQLA server_default).\n- Dart codegen reads/writes the extras passthrough in fromJson/toJson so\n  additionalProperties round-trip instead of dropping unknown keys.\n\n* fix(sync): repr escaping, harvest reindent, update + provenance paths\n\n- apply-bundle _repr_str uses repr() so env/dep values with backslashes or\n  newlines produce a parseable fragments.py (the fast paths skipped escaping).\n- accept-harvested reindents the upstream snippet to the block indent before\n  hashing, so indented merge-blocks round-trip instead of being skipped.\n- a deleted fragment file is classified needs-review, not safe-apply.\n- two-stage layouts re-render the base template first on update (base changes\n  were silently skipped); path-containment uses is_relative_to (component\n  boundaries) so sibling-prefix backends aren''t conflated.\n\n* fix(injectors): newline before splice, anchor-form + tag matching\n\n- python_ast: insert a separating newline before the BEGIN sentinel when the\n  anchor is the last line without a trailing newline (avoids fusing/deleting\n  the anchor); the libcst text-fallback now accepts the # forge:anchor form too.\n- sentinels: anchor the block-tag match so a tag that is a prefix of another\n  cannot match the wrong block.\n\n* fix(cli): dup-column guard, orphan sub-flag gating, auth codemod\n\n- new-entity rejects a user field that collides with a CRUD baseline column\n  (id/created_at/*_id) instead of emitting duplicate columns that fail alembic.\n- orphan verb sub-flags (e.g. --mode without the verb) now error exit 2 rather\n  than silently scaffolding a default project into cwd.\n- the keycloak->platform-auth codemod also rewrites docker-compose.yml env\n  (YAML KEY: value form), not just .env.\n\n* fix(features): redis delays, notif dedupe, data-table, mcp paths\n\n- redis queue: consume() now promotes due messages from the :delayed ZSET, so\n  delay_seconds>0 messages are delivered instead of silently lost.\n- notification store dedupes on stable event id, not the colliding seq field.\n- data-table column-visibility uses the shared container-aware predicate.\n- mcp OpenAPI client percent-encodes path-param values (/ ? # no longer break URLs).\n\n* fix(deploy): provision in-cluster per-backend DBs + ordering\n\nIn-cluster Postgres now creates each backend''s database (init) and the migrate\npre-install hook waits for Postgres, so infra.inCluster=true no longer fails\n''database does not exist''. Drop the dead externalServices config trap.\n\n* fix(generator): place Flutter copier-answers under apps/<slug>/\n\nThe Flutter frontend''s .copier-answers.yml was written to apps/ (parent), so\nforge --update couldn''t find it and silently no-op''d Flutter re-renders.\n\n* fix(matrix): surface skipped verify sub-checks\n\nThe verify lane reported green when uv/cargo/npx were missing because skipped\nbackend checks were dropped from both failures and the skip summary.\n\n* test(golden): refresh snapshots for middleware + auth-guard fixes\n\n* style: satisfy ruff + cargo fmt on batch-2 files\n\nruff (SIM108 ternary in generator.py, format spec.py + migrate codemod) and\ncargo fmt --check on the rust rate_limit middleware. clippy -D warnings was\nalready clean.\n\n* test(golden): refresh rust rate_limit snapshot after fmt\n\n* fix: address #263 cross-review findings\n\n- rust rate limiter is now strictly bounded (LRU-evict the oldest bucket\n  when at capacity and none are idle), matching Python''s hard cap.\n- restore --project-path for the accept-harvested / new-entity / add-backend\n  verbs (the orphan-subflag guard wrongly rejected them).\n- new-entity rejects duplicate user field names (not just baseline collisions).\n- the shared sentinel injector adds a newline before a splice when the marker\n  is the file''s last line without one (parity with the python_ast injector).\n- pydantic string defaults are repr-escaped so quotes/backslashes stay valid.","tree":{"sha":"94eb90a6c4d21c6f78625aa44e0c505fe147f918","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/git/trees/94eb90a6c4d21c6f78625aa44e0c505fe147f918"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/git/commits/b648413f7b6a62930f96efa819090d15cabe5caa","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cchifor/forge/commit/b648413f7b6a62930f96efa819090d15cabe5caa","node_id":"C_kwDOR12LHtoAKGI2NDg0MTNmN2I2YTYyOTMwZjk2ZWZhODE5MDkwZDE1Y2FiZTVjYWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cchifor/forge/commit/b56c292ccfca1d4c92d91a0e150d64c332a0a467","sha":"b56c292ccfca1d4c92d91a0e150d64c332a0a467","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/commits/b56c292ccfca1d4c92d91a0e150d64c332a0a467"}],"sha":"b648413f7b6a62930f96efa819090d15cabe5caa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/commits/b648413f7b6a62930f96efa819090d15cabe5caa"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13657847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cchifor","id":13657847,"login":"cchifor","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNjU3ODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/commits/b56c292ccfca1d4c92d91a0e150d64c332a0a467/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-16T08:45:45Z","email":"chifor@gmail.com","name":"Constantin Chifor"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-16T08:45:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: audit-driven correctness & security remediation (22 bugs) (#262)\n\n* fix(injectors): repair ts-morph helper JS syntax\n\nThe helper embedded a Python f-string `!r` conversion inside a JS\ntemplate literal (`${markerName!r}`), a module-level SyntaxError that\nmade `node` exit non-zero on every invocation. The ts-morph sidecar\ntreats any non-zero exit as ''fall back to regex'', so the opt-in\nFORGE_TS_AST=1 AST-injection path was 100% dead.\n\nUse JSON.stringify for the quoted marker, and harden\ncheck_ts_morph_toolchain to `node --check` the helper so doctor no\nlonger reports a broken helper as healthy.\n\n* fix(sync): collapse CRLF straddling sha256 chunk boundary\n\nprovenance.sha256_of normalized \\r\\n per 64KiB chunk, so a CRLF split\nacross the read boundary survived and diverged from merge.sha256_of_*,\nbreaking the update/harvest round-trip for CRLF files at that size.\n\n* fix(generator): harden registry freeze, inject + layout validation\n\n- feature_loader.load_all now re-raises a FRAGMENT_REGISTRY freeze/audit\n  failure instead of swallowing it and proceeding against an unfrozen,\n  audit-failed registry.\n- plan_validator no longer lets an ''anchor'' key suppress the required\n  target/snippet checks (anchor substitutes for marker only).\n- FrontendConfig.validate rejects layouts whose variant is supported=False\n  (previously selectable via --layout despite being hidden).\n\n* fix(codegen): enum collisions, TS union split, coerce validation\n\n- enums: detect member-name collisions (distinct wire values mangling to\n  one identifier) and build the TS literal union by joining quoted values\n  instead of a '', '' string-replace that split values containing '', ''.\n- openapi binding: validate the transform ''coerce'' kind against the\n  whitelist at binding-validation time (FEATURE_CONTRACT_VIOLATION) rather\n  than aborting later at emit with a generic error.\n\n* fix(gatekeeper): key internal-token cache per credential\n\nThe machine-auth synthetic jti was api-key:<owner>, so two API keys from\none admin (or keys sharing an owner across tenants) collapsed onto one\ncached internal JWT and the first-minted bearer (its roles/tenant) was\nserved to the others — a privilege-escalation / cross-tenant identity\nconfusion bug. Derive the jti from (tenant_id, key_id) per credential,\nmake the test-bypass jti per-tenant, and add a defense-in-depth identity\ncheck so any verified cache hit whose sub/tenant mismatches the request\nis re-minted rather than served.\n\n* fix(gatekeeper): enforce svc- client_id prefix at registry load\n\nThe token-exchange guard blocks user-token exchange via an azp ''svc-''\nprefix check, but the service registry never required it, so a hand-added\nclient without the prefix defeated the guard. Enforce the prefix at load.\n\n* fix(auth-sdk): align Node/Rust wildcard scope matching with Python\n\nNode/Rust authorized <prefix>:* grants via an unbounded prefix match and\nlacked the namespace wildcard, diverging from Python''s segment-bounded\nalgorithm. Synthesize <all-but-last>:* and *:<all-but-first> and test\nexact membership, so all three SDKs make the same authz decision.\n\n* fix(auth-sdk): coerce non-positive S2S expires_in to 300 in Rust\n\nRust used expires_in.unwrap_or(300), leaving an explicit expires_in:0 as a\nzero-second TTL; Python and Node already default <=0 to 300.\n\n* fix(webhooks): add SSRF guard + redirect suppression to Node/Rust\n\nThe Node and Rust webhook delivery paths posted to the user-supplied URL\nwith no host validation and default redirect-follow, the SSRF/open-redirect\nbug the Python sibling was hardened against. Add validate_outbound_url\n(reject non-https, no-host, loopback/link-local/RFC1918/metadata) and\ndisable redirect following, reaching parity with Python.\n\n* fix(flutter): unwrap value.state for deepagent.state_snapshot\n\nThe Flutter chat reducer fed the wrapped {state:{...}} payload straight\ninto AgentState.fromMap, so agent cost/todos/files never rendered and\nlater STATE_DELTA patches targeted the wrong root. Unwrap value[''state'']\nlike the Vue/Svelte reducers.\n\n* fix(multitenancy): bind RLS tenant GUC via set_config\n\nThe shared_rls begin-listener used a parameterized SET LOCAL = %s, which\nPostgres rejects (asyncpg renders $1 -> SQLSTATE 42601), crashing every\nheader/subdomain-resolved transaction. Use the parameter-safe,\ntransaction-local set_config(:guc,:tenant,true) already used by the hook.\n\n* fix(compose): define auth middleware + align host-port validator\n\n- Define the Traefik ''auth'' ForwardAuth middleware (address /auth, identity\n  authResponseHeaders) on the gatekeeper compose fragment; every backend\n  router referenced it but it was defined nowhere, breaking ingress and\n  silently disabling per-request authentication.\n- Reserve the host ports the compose template actually publishes: Postgres\n  15432 (not the container 5432) and pgAdmin 5050 when Postgres renders,\n  Traefik dashboard unconditionally, and Keycloak/Gatekeeper(5000)/Redis\n  under Keycloak. Fixes false rejections (5432) and admitted collisions\n  (15432, gatekeeper 5000, unconditional dashboard).\n\n* fix(deploy): functional in-cluster infra + helm auth parity\n\n- Name the in-cluster Postgres/Redis/Keycloak/Gatekeeper Services with\n  stable literals so they match the hosts baked into workload secretEnv\n  and the cross-service env. Previously they rendered <release>-postgres\n  etc. while secretEnv hardcoded ''postgres'', so infra.inCluster=true failed\n  DNS and aborted the migrate hook (and thus helm install).\n- Carry the keycloak auth env (ENABLED/SERVER_URL/REALM/CLIENT_ID,\n  GATEKEEPER_ISSUER, SERVICE_AUDIENCE) into each Helm workload''s env when\n  keycloak is enabled, mirroring docker-compose; the backend default is\n  auth-off, so k8s deploys previously ran unauthenticated. Realm/client_id\n  are sourced identically to the compose context via compute_topology.\n\n* test(golden): refresh full_feature_max for auth + compose fixes\n\nUpdates the byte-pinned snapshot for the four gatekeeper modules (per-key\ntoken cache, svc- registry prefix) and docker-compose.yml (auth ForwardAuth\nmiddleware). Only the genuinely-changed entries are touched; env-sensitive\nprovenance/generated files keep their committed baseline.\n\n* test: move keycloak fixtures off the gatekeeper 5000 host port\n\nThese fixtures paired include_keycloak with a default-5000 backend, which\nthe host-port validator now correctly rejects (gatekeeper binds 5000).\nUse 5010 so they exercise a bootable config.\n\n* style: satisfy ruff-format + cargo fmt/clippy on audited files\n\nCI lint runs ''ruff format --check forge/'' and the rust verify lane runs\n''cargo fmt --check'' + ''cargo clippy -D warnings''. Reflow doctor.py and the\nhand-written webhooks.rs SSRF helpers, and drop a needless &borrow.\n\n* fix(codegen): reject exact-duplicate enum values\n\nThe collision check only compared distinct wire values, so two identical\nvalues (e.g. [active, active]) emitted the same member twice — uncompilable\nin every target. Reject duplicate values explicitly.","tree":{"sha":"e9359f7724d5476a79a9df0b233f39f8de03aa3c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/git/trees/e9359f7724d5476a79a9df0b233f39f8de03aa3c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/git/commits/b56c292ccfca1d4c92d91a0e150d64c332a0a467","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/we