_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/commits/81e5b842d36f1892ca0a4511097fca72fc72931d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-14T07:07:39Z","email":"chifor@gmail.com","name":"Constantin Chifor"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-14T07:07:39Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(cli): reject unknown top-level config keys (#248)\n\nA typo in a --config file (e.g. `fronend:` for `frontend:`) was silently\ndropped: the loader returns the raw dict, the builder reads only known\nkeys, and validate() never inspected the dict — so the project generated\nwithout that section and forge exited 0, a confidently-wrong result the\nuser discovers only later. _build_config now rejects any unrecognized\ntop-level key with a difflib close-match hint, ahead of the platform-\npreset merge. All three call sites (generate/plan/preview) already\nsurface the ValueError as a clean exit-2 error.","tree":{"sha":"037230cf452ef5aff49a52bce36c492c8c20af4a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/git/trees/037230cf452ef5aff49a52bce36c492c8c20af4a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/git/commits/81e5b842d36f1892ca0a4511097fca72fc72931d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cchifor/forge/commit/81e5b842d36f1892ca0a4511097fca72fc72931d","node_id":"C_kwDOR12LHtoAKDgxZTViODQyZDM2ZjE4OTJjYTBhNDUxMTA5N2ZjYTcyZmM3MjkzMWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cchifor/forge/commit/9ccf021d48cf15b6aaeed2b4f31bcc20a3fb8aa4","sha":"9ccf021d48cf15b6aaeed2b4f31bcc20a3fb8aa4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/commits/9ccf021d48cf15b6aaeed2b4f31bcc20a3fb8aa4"}],"sha":"81e5b842d36f1892ca0a4511097fca72fc72931d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/commits/81e5b842d36f1892ca0a4511097fca72fc72931d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13657847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cchifor","id":13657847,"login":"cchifor","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNjU3ODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/commits/9ccf021d48cf15b6aaeed2b4f31bcc20a3fb8aa4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-14T06:58:31Z","email":"chifor@gmail.com","name":"Constantin Chifor"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-14T06:58:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci(e2e): make nightly e2e job dispatchable (#246)\n\nThe platform compose-boot tests (test_platform_compose_boot.py) run only\nin the e2e-nightly-full job, which was schedule-gated — so a maintainer\ncould not re-run them on demand to confirm a flagship fix without waiting\nup to 24h for the next cron. Gate the job on workflow_dispatch too, and add\nan optional pytest_filter input injected via PYTEST_ADDOPTS for a focused\non-demand run. The run line stays literally unfiltered, so the\ntest_e2e_coverage guard still guarantees the scheduled nightly runs the\nwhole suite.","tree":{"sha":"fa84c82e1d273a60db1d72d35c04781af72088f7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/git/trees/fa84c82e1d273a60db1d72d35c04781af72088f7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/git/commits/9ccf021d48cf15b6aaeed2b4f31bcc20a3fb8aa4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cchifor/forge/commit/9ccf021d48cf15b6aaeed2b4f31bcc20a3fb8aa4","node_id":"C_kwDOR12LHtoAKDljY2YwMjFkNDhjZjE1YjZhYWVlZDJiNGYzMWJjYzIwYTNmYjhhYTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cchifor/forge/commit/17609cd8d904ab3434bd28929ede7e77b1529363","sha":"17609cd8d904ab3434bd28929ede7e77b1529363","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/commits/17609cd8d904ab3434bd28929ede7e77b1529363"}],"sha":"9ccf021d48cf15b6aaeed2b4f31bcc20a3fb8aa4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/commits/9ccf021d48cf15b6aaeed2b4f31bcc20a3fb8aa4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13657847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cchifor","id":13657847,"login":"cchifor","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNjU3ODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/commits/17609cd8d904ab3434bd28929ede7e77b1529363/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-13T11:57:11Z","email":"chifor@gmail.com","name":"Constantin Chifor"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-13T11:57:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(generator): supply project_title for two-stage variants (#245)\n\nA two-stage application-template variant (e.g. tenant-management-service)\nrenders an overlay with its own copier.yml that declares no questions, so\nit never computed copier''s project_title when:false default — the overlay''s\nconfig/default.yaml rendered title: \"\" and the generated FastAPI app\ncrashed at boot (\"A title must be provided for OpenAPI\"). This was the\nchronic multitenant-saas nightly compose-boot failure: the tms control-plane\nservice crash-looped, so it never reached healthy.\n\nSupply project_title from variable_mapper.backend_context so every render\nstage gets it. Built-in single-stage renders are byte-identical (value\nmatches copier''s computed default; golden snapshots unchanged). Validated:\nthe regenerated tms service boots healthy. Add a regression test on the\ntenant-management-service variant''s rendered title.","tree":{"sha":"b60964dee7693e926db1c14448be6db2d17fc350","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/git/trees/b60964dee7693e926db1c14448be6db2d17fc350"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/git/commits/17609cd8d904ab3434bd28929ede7e77b1529363","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cchifor/forge/commit/17609cd8d904ab3434bd28929ede7e77b1529363","node_id":"C_kwDOR12LHtoAKDE3NjA5Y2Q4ZDkwNGFiMzQzNGJkMjg5MjllZGU3ZTc3YjE1MjkzNjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cchifor/forge/commit/34e7e1790f097d192bc3a69e1918588783c77b21","sha":"34e7e1790f097d192bc3a69e1918588783c77b21","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/commits/34e7e1790f097d192bc3a69e1918588783c77b21"}],"sha":"17609cd8d904ab3434bd28929ede7e77b1529363","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/commits/17609cd8d904ab3434bd28929ede7e77b1529363"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13657847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cchifor","id":13657847,"login":"cchifor","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNjU3ODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/commits/34e7e1790f097d192bc3a69e1918588783c77b21/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-13T09:52:47Z","email":"chifor@gmail.com","name":"Constantin Chifor"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-13T09:52:47Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(deploy): k8s/Helm port tracks server_port (#244)\n\nGenerated raw k8s manifests hardcoded containerPort: 8000 while the\nbackend listens on the configured server_port (default 5000), so the\nliveness/readiness probes — which target the named http port — failed\nfor any non-8000 project. Templatize containerPort from {{ server_port }}\n(deployment.yaml -> .jinja, per-backend so each gets its real port), and\nthread the primary backend''s port into the project-scope render context\nso the Helm chart''s values.yaml targetPort default follows it too. Health\npaths already matched the Dockerfile HEALTHCHECK. Add a regression test\non a non-default port.","tree":{"sha":"1b7ce3b6282ef32bffd237a19f4c2922f73b67a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/git/trees/1b7ce3b6282ef32bffd237a19f4c2922f73b67a3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/git/commits/34e7e1790f097d192bc3a69e1918588783c77b21","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cchifor/forge/commit/34e7e1790f097d192bc3a69e1918588783c77b21","node_id":"C_kwDOR12LHtoAKDM0ZTdlMTc5MGYwOTdkMTkyYmMzYTY5ZTE5MTg1ODg3ODNjNzdiMjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cchifor/forge/commit/9022ca9d51700e31ba711c5bd52c779e728b237e","sha":"9022ca9d51700e31ba711c5bd52c779e728b237e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/commits/9022ca9d51700e31ba711c5bd52c779e728b237e"}],"sha":"34e7e1790f097d192bc3a69e1918588783c77b21","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/commits/34e7e1790f097d192bc3a69e1918588783c77b21"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13657847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cchifor","id":13657847,"login":"cchifor","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNjU3ODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/commits/9022ca9d51700e31ba711c5bd52c779e728b237e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-13T09:41:59Z","email":"chifor@gmail.com","name":"Constantin Chifor"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-13T09:41:59Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore: remove never-adopted PortSpec/service_registration seam (#243)\n\nThe Pillar A.4 / RFC-009 renderer scaffolding had zero consumers — no\nFragment ever populated a PortSpec, and the shared ports/mod.rs collision\nit was meant to solve was handled by inject.yaml markers (#236) instead.\n\nDelete forge/service_registration.py, forge/specs/port.py, the\n_shared/service_registration + _shared/port_spec templates, and their\ntests; drop the PortSpec re-exports from forge.specs / forge.appliers;\nmark RFC-009 superseded. The generic FragmentRenderer protocol and\nMiddlewareSpec (its sole live implementer via Fragment.middlewares) and\nall docstrings are kept/cleaned.","tree":{"sha":"d8aba63e0e208470f9a7548758a0fdfcd0fb0c63","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/git/trees/d8aba63e0e208470f9a7548758a0fdfcd0fb0c63"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/git/commits/9022ca9d51700e31ba711c5bd52c779e728b237e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cchifor/forge/commit/9022ca9d51700e31ba711c5bd52c779e728b237e","node_id":"C_kwDOR12LHtoAKDkwMjJjYTlkNTE3MDBlMzFiYTcxMWM1YmQ1MmM3NzllNzI4YjIzN2U","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cchifor/forge/commit/1e4a4ea3bbc942936650ab223d1f97141fff9de1","sha":"1e4a4ea3bbc942936650ab223d1f97141fff9de1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/commits/1e4a4ea3bbc942936650ab223d1f97141fff9de1"}],"sha":"9022ca9d51700e31ba711c5bd52c779e728b237e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/commits/9022ca9d51700e31ba711c5bd52c779e728b237e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13657847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cchifor","id":13657847,"login":"cchifor","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNjU3ODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/commits/1e4a4ea3bbc942936650ab223d1f97141fff9de1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-13T07:23:06Z","email":"chifor@gmail.com","name":"Constantin Chifor"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-13T07:23:06Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(plugins): make add_frontend genuinely generate (#241)\n\n* feat(plugins): make add_frontend genuinely generate\n\nThe frontend twin of #224''s add_backend fix. A plugin-registered\nfrontend framework used to crash (No mapper in variable_mapper) or\nrender nothing (_generate_frontend knew only the built-in TEMPLATE_DIRS).\nThe frontend dispatch now consults FRONTEND_SPECS for plugin frameworks:\n\n- variable_mapper: a generic plugin_frontend_context (no per-framework\n  mapper) instead of raising.\n- generator: _generate_frontend template-dir lookup + the forge.toml\n  writer fall back to the FrontendSpec''s template_dir.\n- docker_manager: a node_based plugin frontend gets the npm-workspace\n  root + Node Dockerfile with build_dir/package_manager from the spec\n  (new FrontendSpec fields).\n- CLI: --frontend choices + the interactive prompt build after plugin\n  load; config-file frontend.framework resolves via\n  resolve_frontend_framework instead of silently coercing to none.\n- updater: --update resolves a plugin frontend from the manifest instead\n  of dropping it to NONE.\n\nShip examples/forge-vite-frontend (a Vite vanilla-TS reference) +\ntests/test_plugin_frontend_vite.py, which generates the SPA and builds\nit (npm install + npm run build -> dist/).\n\n* fix(plugins): address add_frontend review\n\nCodex review of the add_frontend work:\n- non-node_based plugin frontends no longer get forge''s Node Dockerfile +\n  nginx (they ship their own deploy assets); forge renders deploy only for\n  built-ins and node_based plugin frontends.\n- a headless/config-driven plugin frontend now defaults its package manager\n  from FrontendSpec.package_manager (parity with the interactive prompt),\n  not a hardcoded npm.\n- layout validation now covers any framework with registered layout variants\n  (a plugin that ships layouts), not just the built-ins.\n\n* test(plugins): resolve npm via which for Windows\n\nsubprocess.run([\"npm\", ...]) fails on Windows (npm is npm.cmd; Python\ndoesn''t walk PATHEXT for a bare name). Resolve it with shutil.which —\nthe same fix forge''s _run_backend_cmd already uses — so the vite-frontend\nbuild e2e runs on the Windows test lane.","tree":{"sha":"9fac4b3f5da83aacebbe6f2afe44bb9492b5718e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/git/trees/9fac4b3f5da83aacebbe6f2afe44bb9492b5718e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/git/commits/1e4a4ea3bbc942936650ab223d1f97141fff9de1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cchifor/forge/commit/1e4a4ea3bbc942936650ab223d1f97141fff9de1","node_id":"C_kwDOR12LHtoAKDFlNGE0ZWEzYmJjOTQyOTM2NjUwYWIyMjNkMWY5NzE0MWZmZjlkZTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cchifor/forge/commit/fc08ce3fe85283ec45e8528f2b0e1f46881b136b","sha":"fc08ce3fe85283ec45e8528f2b0e1f46881b136b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/commits/fc08ce3fe85283ec45e8528f2b0e1f46881b136b"}],"sha":"1e4a4ea3bbc942936650ab223d1f97141fff9de1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/commits/1e4a4ea3bbc942936650ab223d1f97141fff9de1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13657847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cchifor","id":13657847,"login":"cchifor","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNjU3ODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/commits/fc08ce3fe85283ec45e8528f2b0e1f46881b136b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-12T19:50:47Z","email":"chifor@gmail.com","name":"Constantin Chifor"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-12T19:50:47Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(rust): share ports/adapters mod.rs; fix apalis consumer (#240)\n\n* fix(rust): share ports/adapters mod.rs; fix apalis consumer\n\n#236: llm_port/llm_openai injected a full src/ports/mod.rs and\nsrc/adapters/mod.rs that overwrote the base template''s shared files, so\neven an llm-only Rust project failed to generate and a conflicts_with\nmutex blocked llm+queue/cache. They now inject pub mod llm; / pub mod\nllm_openai; into the shared mod.rs like queue/cache — mutex retired,\nall ports coexist.\n\n#235: the apalis queue consumer called the private RedisStorage::\nfetch_next; rewritten against apalis 0.6''s public WorkerBuilder API (a\nbackground worker forwards jobs into a channel the consume() stream\ndrains). Dropped the unused Pin import; rustfmt''d the latent fmt drift\nin the apalis/cache/llm/queue Rust fragments now that rust_ports\nverifies them.\n\nrust_ports matrix scenario broadened to llm+apalis+cache+webhooks\n(build+clippy+fmt all green locally).\n\n* fix(rust): wire apalis ack/nack via disposition handshake\n\nAddress codex review of the apalis consumer:\n- drive the apalis worker INLINE in the consume() stream (not a detached\n  tokio::spawn) so dropping the stream stops the worker — no leaked task,\n  and an un-acked in-flight message is redelivered, not falsely acked.\n- the worker handler now blocks on a per-message disposition the consumer\n  signals via ack/nack (a oneshot keyed by receipt), mapping onto apalis''s\n  job outcome: Ok=ack, Error::Failed=requeue, Error::Abort=dead-letter. So\n  the QueuePort ack/nack contract holds instead of auto-acking at handoff.\n\nAlso update test_capability_resolver: rust llm+cache now coexist (the #236\nshared-mod.rs injection retired the Rust-only conflict mutex).\n\n* fix(rust): unique apalis consumer id; cover conflict_backends\n\nCodex follow-up:\n- make the apalis worker name unique per consume() (append a UUID) so the\n  Redis consumer identity doesn''t collide across stream instances /\n  replicas, which would confuse orphan recovery for in-flight jobs.\n- correct the drop-semantics comments (a stream dropped after hand-over\n  relies on apalis orphan recovery, not an immediate requeue) and note\n  ack needs the stream to keep being polled.\n\nAdd a synthetic-fragment unit test for the backend-scoped conflict\nresolver path (conflict_backends) — #236 retired the only built-in users\n(llm_port/llm_openai), so the mechanism needs direct coverage.","tree":{"sha":"4db9bc7b30b9932be0e0b906f684200b0c14a6c9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/git/trees/4db9bc7b30b9932be0e0b906f684200b0c14a6c9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/git/commits/fc08ce3fe85283ec45e8528f2b0e1f46881b136b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cchifor/forge/commit/fc08ce3fe85283ec45e8528f2b0e1f46881b136b","node_id":"C_kwDOR12LHtoAKGZjMDhjZTNmZTg1MjgzZWM0NWU4NTI4ZjJiMGUxZjQ2ODgxYjEzNmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cchifor/forge/commit/c9bf34b8f508267b7aa5c3c42b5625146a53ae40","sha":"c9bf34b8f508267b7aa5c3c42b5625146a53ae40","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/commits/c9bf34b8f508267b7aa5c3c42b5625146a53ae40"}],"sha":"fc08ce3fe85283ec45e8528f2b0e1f46881b136b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/commits/fc08ce3fe85283ec45e8528f2b0e1f46881b136b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13657847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cchifor","id":13657847,"login":"cchifor","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNjU3ODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/commits/c9bf34b8f508267b7aa5c3c42b5625146a53ae40/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-12T17:36:32Z","email":"chifor@gmail.com","name":"Constantin Chifor"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-12T17:36:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(plugins): make add_backend generate real projects (#239)\n\n* feat(plugins): make add_backend generate real projects\n\nResolve plugin-registered backend languages through resolve_backend_\nlanguage at the five sites that coerced the language string via\nBackendLanguage(...) and crashed on anything but python/node/rust\n(forge.toml writer, config-file parser, add-backend command, --update\ntemplate-version walk, variable-mapper context). add_backend now seeds\nthe language''s default crud-service variant so a BackendConfig validates\nout of the box, and the CLI builds --backend-language choices after\nplugin load.\n\nShip examples/forge-go-backend as the reference: a plugin that registers\na Go (net/http) backend language end to end (package-data template,\nabsolute template_dir, BackendToolchain). tests/test_plugin_backend_go.py\ngenerates and compiles it.\n\nCloses #224.\n\n* test(plugins): make go-backend fixture idempotent\n\nThe plugin-e2e job pip-installs forge-go-backend, so load_all already\nregisters ''go'' via the entry point before the fixture runs — re-calling\nregister() tripped the collision guard. Detect an existing registration\nand reuse it (no re-register, no scrub) so the suite runs whether or not\nthe plugin is installed.\n\n* fix(plugins): close plugin-backend gaps from review\n\nAddress codex review of the add_backend work:\n- root compose no longer emits a migrate sidecar for a stateless plugin\n  backend (would deadlock docker compose up on service_completed_successfully)\n- interactive backend prompt builds BackendConfig with known fields only,\n  so a plugin version field (go_version) no longer raises TypeError\n- --update backend scan infers plugin backends from .copier-answers _src_path\n- pin the plugin version field in the template context (copier-answers) via\n  spec.version_choices[0], decoupling the Go module floor (go 1.19) from the\n  recommended toolchain (go_version, Docker builder image)\n- render the reference Go .gitignore (was emitting the literal Jinja token)\n\n* fix(plugins): harden interactive + update for plugin backends\n\nSecond review pass:\n- interactive prompt no longer asks for a plugin backend''s version when\n  there''s nowhere to store it (asking then dropping the answer misled);\n  the template''s own default applies.\n- --update fails loud when a services/<name> dir is a forge-rendered\n  backend (has copier-answers _src_path) but maps to no loaded backend,\n  instead of silently dropping it from the regenerated forge.toml.\n\n* fix(ci): pin setup-go to SHA, satisfy ruff\n\n- pin actions/setup-go to v5.6.0 SHA (workflow-pinning policy test)\n- ruff import-sort + format on the reference plugin and touched files\n- restructure the go-backend fixture cleanup to avoid return-in-finally (B012)","tree":{"sha":"46d09c1d242a4869eb511ae8747c2f545afd5fd2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/git/trees/46d09c1d242a4869eb511ae8747c2f545afd5fd2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/git/commits/c9bf34b8f508267b7aa5c3c42b5625146a53ae40","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cchifor/forge/commit/c9bf34b8f508267b7aa5c3c42b5625146a53ae40","node_id":"C_kwDOR12LHtoAKGM5YmYzNGI4ZjUwODI2N2I3YWE1YzNjNDJiNTYyNTE0NmE1M2FlNDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cchifor/forge/commit/deab728b908f496ea7d34cd1f1ff7a2241c0d25c","sha":"deab728b908f496ea7d34cd1f1ff7a2241c0d25c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/commits/deab728b908f496ea7d34cd1f1ff7a2241c0d25c"}],"sha":"c9bf34b8f508267b7aa5c3c42b5625146a53ae40","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/commits/c9bf34b8f508267b7aa5c3c42b5625146a53ae40"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13657847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cchifor","id":13657847,"login":"cchifor","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNjU3ODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/commits/deab728b908f496ea7d34cd1f1ff7a2241c0d25c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-12T16:12:17Z","email":"chifor@gmail.com","name":"Constantin Chifor"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-12T16:12:17Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(generator): commit lockfiles, install frozen in images (#238)\n\n* feat(generator): commit lockfiles, install frozen in images\n\nResolve a workspace-root package-lock.json / Cargo.lock at generation\ntime and switch the service Dockerfiles to npm ci / cargo build --locked\n(falling back to unlocked installs when no lockfile was resolved). Builds\nnow pin the exact transitive versions forge resolved instead of drifting\nwith registry HEAD.\n\nCloses #223.\n\n* feat(generator): freeze frontend image + generated CI installs\n\nAddress codex review of #223: the frontend Docker image and the\ngenerated node/rust CI workflows also install frozen now (npm ci /\n<pm> install --frozen-lockfile / cargo --locked, each with a graceful\nfallback when no lockfile is committed). Closes the gap where a stale\nlockfile could pass generated CI yet fail the prod Docker build.","tree":{"sha":"7d39560a7cb0060e4b4f197bba747058b0403c9a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/git/trees/7d39560a7cb0060e4b4f197bba747058b0403c9a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/git/commits/deab728b908f496ea7d34cd1f1ff7a2241c0d25c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cchifor/forge/commit/deab728b908f496ea7d34cd1f1ff7a2241c0d25c","node_id":"C_kwDOR12LHtoAKGRlYWI3MjhiOTA4ZjQ5NmVhN2QzNGNkMWYxZmY3YTIyNDFjMGQyNWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cchifor/forge/commit/fb429f3f45c63a55668dec2b36ca568610a2af14","sha":"fb429f3f45c63a55668dec2b36ca568610a2af14","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/commits/fb429f3f45c63a55668dec2b36ca568610a2af14"}],"sha":"deab728b908f496ea7d34cd1f1ff7a2241c0d25c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/commits/deab728b908f496ea7d34cd1f1ff7a2241c0d25c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13657847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cchifor","id":13657847,"login":"cchifor","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNjU3ODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/commits/fb429f3f45c63a55668dec2b36ca568610a2af14/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-12T15:24:23Z","email":"chifor@gmail.com","name":"Constantin Chifor"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-12T15:24:23Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: compile generated node/rust ports in CI (#213) (#237)\n\nTri-language port parity was asserted only by string-matching; the\ngenerated Node/Rust port adapters never actually compiled in CI. Add two\nmatrix scenarios in lanes [generate, verify] that enable the real port\nadapters so `tsc --noEmit` / `cargo build` run on them — and fix the three\ndefects they immediately surfaced:\n\n- **node_ports** (queue=bullmq + response_cache + llm=openai + webhooks):\n  the `llm_openai` Node adapter typed `toAiTools` as `Record<string, unknown>`,\n  which AI SDK 4 rejects (`streamText` wants `tools?: ToolSet`). Wrap each\n  schema with `jsonSchema()` and return `ToolSet`. Now passes biome + tsc +\n  vitest.\n- **rust_ports** (webhooks): the base rust `routes/mod.rs.jinja` mentioned the\n  `FORGE:ROUTES_NESTED_REGISTRATION` marker token in a doc comment AND used it\n  as the injection marker, so the unique-marker injector found it twice and\n  any fragment injecting there (webhooks) failed generation. Reword the doc\n  comment. Also rustfmt the webhooks Rust fragment files (they shipped\n  unformatted, failing `cargo fmt --check`). Now passes build + fmt + clippy +\n  test.\n\nTwo deeper Rust-port defects #213 surfaced are filed for focused fixes\n(they need a public-API rewrite / the PortSpec migration), so `rust_ports`\ndeliberately scopes to webhooks for now: apalis calls a private apalis-redis\nmethod (#235); llm + webhooks both write `src/ports/mod.rs` (#236).","tree":{"sha":"0b8c2df29c3848e2092650e4d71ef050874c5138","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/git/trees/0b8c2df29c3848e2092650e4d71ef050874c5138"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/git/commits/fb429f3f45c63a55668dec2b36ca568610a2af14","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cchifor/forge/commit/fb429f3f45c63a55668dec2b36ca568610a2af14","node_id":"C_kwDOR12LHtoAKGZiNDI5ZjNmNDVjNjNhNTU2NjhkZWMyYjM2Y2E1Njg2MTBhMmFmMTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cchifor/forge/commit/94cd527c4c8b982f1cad5dc83e1e8a6f5dec6bf6","sha":"94cd527c4c8b982f1cad5dc83e1e8a6f5dec6bf6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/commits/94cd527c4c8b982f1cad5dc83e1e8a6f5dec6bf6"}],"sha":"fb429f3f45c63a55668dec2b36ca568610a2af14","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/commits/fb429f3f45c63a55668dec2b36ca568610a2af14"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13657847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cchifor","id":13657847,"login":"cchifor","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNjU3ODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/commits/94cd527c4c8b982f1cad5dc83e1e8a6f5dec6bf6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-12T14:02:31Z","email":"chifor@gmail.com","name":"Constantin Chifor"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-12T14:02:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(deps): pin floating pgadmin/uv base images (#223) (#234)\n\nGenerated projects pulled `dpage/pgadmin4:latest` (4 compose templates)\nand the worker Dockerfile copied uv from `ghcr.io/astral-sh/uv:latest` —\nboth float, so a pgadmin/uv release could silently change or break a\ndev stack.\n\n- pgadmin → `dpage/pgadmin4:9` (verified tag; matches the existing\n  `postgres:16-alpine` / `redis:7-alpine` major-tag convention).\n- worker uv stage → `ghcr.io/astral-sh/uv:0.11.16`, matching the main\n  service Dockerfile (which was already pinned) — they were inconsistent.\n\nGoldens regenerated (only the two compose files'' sha changes). Lockfiles\n+ full digest-pinning of the already-tag-pinned images remain a larger\nfollow-up under #223.","tree":{"sha":"829057ad1988e0e27ae6c796fe84de48d41fb382","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/git/trees/829057ad1988e0e27ae6c796fe84de48d41fb382"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/git/commits/94cd527c4c8b982f1cad5dc83e1e8a6f5dec6bf6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cchifor/forge/commit/94cd527c4c8b982f1cad5dc83e1e8a6f5dec6bf6","node_id":"C_kwDOR12LHtoAKDk0Y2Q1MjdjNGM4Yjk4MmYxY2FkNWRjODNlMWU4YTZmNWRlYzZiZjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cchifor/forge/commit/b4573395026c629cd40b691335948bf226fd9e35","sha":"b4573395026c629cd40b691335948bf226fd9e35","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/commits/b4573395026c629cd40b691335948bf226fd9e35"}],"sha":"94cd527c4c8b982f1cad5dc83e1e8a6f5dec6bf6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/commits/94cd527c4c8b982f1cad5dc83e1e8a6f5dec6bf6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13657847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cchifor","id":13657847,"login":"cchifor","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNjU3ODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/commits/b4573395026c629cd40b691335948bf226fd9e35/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-12T13:34:49Z","email":"chifor@gmail.com","name":"Constantin Chifor"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-12T13:34:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci: notify maintainers on nightly failure (#217) (#233)\n\n* ci: notify maintainers on nightly failure (#217)\n\nA failed scheduled nightly died silently in the Actions tab — the exact\nway regressions ship unnoticed. Add a notify-on-failure job to both\nheavyweight scheduled nightlies (matrix-nightly + the unfiltered\ne2e-nightly-full lane) that opens (or comments on) a shared\n`nightly-failure` tracking issue, so a red nightly is visible.\n\n- Schedule-only (`github.event_name == ''schedule''`) so PR / dispatch /\n  label runs never open issues; fires on lane failure; `issues: write`.\n- De-dupes onto one open \"Nightly CI failed\" issue (find-or-create).\n- tests/test_nightly_notifications.py mechanizes the guard so the\n  notifier can''t be silently dropped by a future workflow edit.\n\nThe other #217 symptoms are already resolved: the dashboard''s\nmerge-multiple download + empty-state guard no longer drop smoke\nresults or double-run a lane, and docs/matrix-status.md is a\nby-design manual snapshot (live data is the job summary + the\nmatrix-status-grid artifact). Closes #217.\n\n* ci: fix notifier jq + cover prerequisite failures\n\nAddress codex review of #233:\n\n- Blocker: `gh issue list --jq ''.[0].number''` emits the string \"null\" (not\n  empty) when no issue exists, so the find-or-create test `[ -n ... ]` was\n  always true and would `gh issue comment \"null\"`. Use `// empty`.\n- Harden: a failed prerequisite skips the work job (result ''skipped'', not\n  ''failure''), so a broken `gate` (matrix-nightly) or `e2e-core` (e2e) would\n  notify nobody. Watch both — add them to `needs` + the failure condition.\n- Strengthen the guard test to assert the prerequisite is covered.","tree":{"sha":"6756db2f8d2ae3cce5b9d2f5c086afb92927b8ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/git/trees/6756db2f8d2ae3cce5b9d2f5c086afb92927b8ae"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/git/commits/b4573395026c629cd40b691335948bf226fd9e35","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cchifor/forge/commit/b4573395026c629cd40b691335948bf226fd9e35","node_id":"C_kwDOR12LHtoAKGI0NTczMzk1MDI2YzYyOWNkNDBiNjkxMzM1OTQ4YmYyMjZmZDllMzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cchifor/forge/commit/186d464f057da7102bcc453dacb4501db676667c","sha":"186d464f057da7102bcc453dacb4501db676667c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/commits/186d464f057da7102bcc453dacb4501db676667c"}],"sha":"b4573395026c629cd40b691335948bf226fd9e35","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/commits/b4573395026c629cd40b691335948bf226fd9e35"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13657847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cchifor","id":13657847,"login":"cchifor","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNjU3ODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/commits/186d464f057da7102bcc453dacb4501db676667c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-12T07:58:21Z","email":"chifor@gmail.com","name":"Constantin Chifor"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-12T07:58:21Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(canvas): resolve reducer split-brain (#214) (#232)\n\nThe standalone packages/canvas-core reducer drifted from the vendored\ntemplate copies that generated projects actually receive (aliased via\nvite.config / svelte.config). It never got the snake_case `tool_call_id`\nuser-prompt fix (5b27264): it read camelCase `toolCallId` only, emitted\n`toolCallId`, and used the old `{ id, label }` option shape. Meanwhile the\ncross-stack contract guard pointed AT the stale package, so it validated\ndead code while the vendored copies users get went unguarded.\n\n- Back-port the canonical reducer.ts + snapshot.ts from the vendored copy\n  into packages/canvas-core (snake_case `tool_call_id` primary + camelCase\n  fallback, `{ label, description?, recommended? }` options,\n  `pendingPrompt.tool_call_id`). The two files are now byte-identical to the\n  vendored source again.\n- Retarget the reducer constants in test_chat_tool_call_args_contract.py\n  from packages/canvas-core to the vendored Vue/Svelte copies, so the guard\n  protects the code users actually receive.\n- Add tests/test_canvas_vendored_parity.py: a pure-Python static guard that\n  the Vue and Svelte vendored canvas-core trees stay byte-identical, the\n  user-prompt path stays snake_case, and TOOL_CALL_* streaming stays\n  camelCase (TS + Flutter) — matching the pydantic-ai wire.\n- Fix two now-stale packages vitest expectations: the user_prompt test fed\n  the old camelCase/`id` shape, and a \"TOOL_CALL_ARGS is a no-op\" test\n  predated the args-buffering the contract test already requires.\n\nNot deleting packages/ — it''s an active npm workspace with live CI/probe\nconsumers and codegen targets; back-porting eliminates the split-brain\nwithout that larger refactor. Validated: 157 Python canvas tests pass;\ncanvas-core (72) + canvas-vue (7) vitest + typechecks pass on node 22.\n\nCloses #214.","tree":{"sha":"8048fc58d2322a716a72c580d046808378d0a19f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/git/trees/8048fc58d2322a716a72c580d046808378d0a19f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/git/commits/186d464f057da7102bcc453dacb4501db676667c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cchifor/forge/commit/186d464f057da7102bcc453dacb4501db676667c","node_id":"C_kwDOR12LHtoAKDE4NmQ0NjRmMDU3ZGE3MTAyYmNjNDUzZGFjYjQ1MDFkYjY3NjY2N2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cchifor/forge/commit/cbcec4c7043ed2cc5fdd5eb58b1ac3d42fdbf749","sha":"cbcec4c7043ed2cc5fdd5eb58b1ac3d42fdbf749","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/commits/cbcec4c7043ed2cc5fdd5eb58b1ac3d42fdbf749"}],"sha":"186d464f057da7102bcc453dacb4501db676667c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/commits/186d464f057da7102bcc453dacb4501db676667c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13657847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cchifor","id":13657847,"login":"cchifor","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNjU3ODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/commits/cbcec4c7043ed2cc5fdd5eb58b1ac3d42fdbf749/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-12T04:00:46Z","email":"chifor@gmail.com","name":"Constantin Chifor"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-12T04:00:46Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore: switch to GitHub-only distribution (#231)\n\n* chore: switch to GitHub-only distribution\n\nforge is no longer published to any package registry (PyPI/npm/pub.dev).\nSource stays on GitHub; the canonical install is `./install`, which runs\n`uv tool install git+<repo>`.\n\n- release.yml: drop the dry-run gate and all five registry-publish jobs\n  (pypi/npm-canvas-vue/-svelte/pub-dev-core/pub-dev); keep a standalone\n  github-release that builds sdist+wheel, generates a CycloneDX SBOM, and\n  cuts a GitHub Release with the changelog notes — still gated by the\n  tag<->version check. No `release` env, NPM_AUTH_TOKEN, PUB_DEV_CREDENTIALS,\n  or PyPI trusted-publisher needed.\n- Delete release-dryrun.yml — its only purpose was rehearsing registry\n  publishing + feeding the removed dry-run gate.\n- Fix the macOS install-script abort: the uv installer exits non-zero in a\n  non-interactive shell, which under `set -o pipefail`/`set -e` killed the\n  installer right after a successful install. The `installed uv` re-check is\n  authoritative, so ignore the installer''s exit code; also harden get_version.\n- Docs: rewrite RELEASING.md for the GitHub-only flow; mark RFC-003\n  superseded; fix the PyPI install instructions in GETTING_STARTED + the\n  plugin-install line in README; CHANGELOG entry.\n\nThe OPERATIONAL_RUNBOOK \"botched release recovery\" section (registry-publish\nspecific) is now obsolete — left for a focused doc follow-up.\n\n* fix(install): drop errexit for macOS bash 3.2\n\nThe earlier `|| true` guards didn''t fix the macOS install abort — it still\ndied right after a successful uv install. Root cause: macOS ships bash 3.2,\nwhose `set -e`/`set -o pipefail`/`|| true` interaction aborts the script even\non guarded commands, and the uv installer exits non-zero non-interactively.\n\nDrop `errexit` entirely (keep `nounset` + `pipefail`) — this is a bootstrap\ninstaller whose steps return non-zero by design. The two things that matter,\nuv and forge, are now verified explicitly with `if ! installed ...; exit 1`.\nAlso `--force` the forge install so re-runs are idempotent.\n\n* docs: scrub release-pipeline refs for GitHub-only\n\nCodex impl-review flagged that deleting the publish pipeline left stale\nregistry-recovery instructions that would mislead a maintainer.\n\n- OPERATIONAL_RUNBOOK §1 \"botched release recovery\" rewritten for the\n  GitHub-only model (a failed `github-release` job, not a partial registry\n  publish); §4.3 pre-publish-gates collapsed to the single github-release job;\n  CI-triage workflow list + changelog-extract note corrected.\n- troubleshooting: \"release-dryrun/ok blocked\" section replaced with the\n  GitHub-Release failure modes; dropped a stale \"Release dry-run\" pointer.\n- MAINTAINER_ONBOARDING release cadence updated.\n- RFC-004 (release rehearsal) marked superseded.\n- extract-changelog.sh comment no longer references the deleted workflow.\n\n* fix(install): verify uv-tool exit code + resolve bin dir\n\nCodex review of the errexit-drop hardening flagged two latent gaps:\n\n- Without errexit, `uv tool install`''s exit code was ignored, so a failed\n  install combined with a pre-existing `forge` on PATH (e.g. Foundry''s\n  `forge`) would report false success. Capture `PIPESTATUS[0]` and fail on\n  nonzero.\n- The verify hardcoded `~/.local/bin`, ignoring uv''s configurable tool bin\n  dir (`UV_TOOL_BIN_DIR` / `XDG_BIN_HOME`). Resolve it via `uv tool dir\n  --bin` and prepend it so the uv-installed forge wins; warn (non-Windows)\n  if a different `forge` still shadows ours.\n\nValidated: `bash install` runs clean end-to-end locally (exit 0).","tree":{"sha":"7d0b6ee219e111a8793a324124b3018284228e05","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/git/trees/7d0b6ee219e111a8793a324124b3018284228e05"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/git/commits/cbcec4c7043ed2cc5fdd5eb58b1ac3d42fdbf749","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cchifor/forge/commit/cbcec4c7043ed2cc5fdd5eb58b1ac3d42fdbf749","node_id":"C_kwDOR12LHtoAKGNiY2VjNGM3MDQzZWQyY2M1ZmRkNWViNThiMWFjM2Q0MmZkYmY3NDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cchifor/forge/commit/562115ebeb80f15796481adf8c87cd931266dab0","sha":"562115ebeb80f15796481adf8c87cd931266dab0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/commits/562115ebeb80f15796481adf8c87cd931266dab0"}],"sha":"cbcec4c7043ed2cc5fdd5eb58b1ac3d42fdbf749","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/commits/cbcec4c7043ed2cc5fdd5eb58b1ac3d42fdbf749"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13657847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cchifor","id":13657847,"login":"cchifor","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNjU3ODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/commits/562115ebeb80f15796481adf8c87cd931266dab0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-11T01:29:20Z","email":"chifor@gmail.com","name":"Constantin Chifor"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-11T01:29:20Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test(e2e): prove a chat turn at runtime via AG-UI SSE (#230)\n\n* test(e2e): prove a chat turn at runtime via AG-UI SSE\n\nEvery chat lane to date was static (typecheck / wire-format / render);\nno test ever ran an actual chat turn. This scaffolds an `agent.llm`\nproject, `uv sync`s it, boots the app in-process, and drives one turn\nthrough the canonical AG-UI SSE endpoint (POST /api/v1/agent), asserting\nthe reduced `RUN_STARTED -> TEXT_MESSAGE_* -> RUN_FINISHED` sequence.\n\nNo LLM, no Postgres: the model is stubbed with pydantic-ai''s\ndeterministic `TestModel` (the endpoint imports `build_agent` lazily per\nrequest, so patching the module attribute needs no template change), and\nthe app defaults to `sqlite+aiosqlite` with in-process table creation, so\n`TestClient` boots the full stack with no external services.\n\nMarked `e2e` (runs in the unfiltered nightly lane) and `require_uv`\n(skips cleanly without uv). Satisfies the GA exit criterion \"chat turn\nproven at runtime in CI\". Closes #212.\n\n* test(e2e): assert AG-UI envelope order, not just presence","tree":{"sha":"d246c64f94c8fa19938892827fdc7391a3fffba7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/git/trees/d246c64f94c8fa19938892827fdc7391a3fffba7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/git/commits/562115ebeb80f15796481adf8c87cd931266dab0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cchifor/forge/commit/562115ebeb80f15796481adf8c87cd931266dab0","node_id":"C_kwDOR12LHtoAKDU2MjExNWViZWI4MGYxNTc5NjQ4MWFkZjhjODdjZDkzMTI2NmRhYjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cchifor/forge/commit/57adc58c2a9bf85a3843064c77beaa57d8ec6932","sha":"57adc58c2a9bf85a3843064c77beaa57d8ec6932","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/commits/57adc58c2a9bf85a3843064c77beaa57d8ec6932"}],"sha":"562115ebeb80f15796481adf8c87cd931266dab0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/commits/562115ebeb80f15796481adf8c87cd931266dab0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13657847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cchifor","id":13657847,"login":"cchifor","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNjU3ODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cchifor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/commits/57adc58c2a9bf85a3843064c77beaa57d8ec6932/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-11T00:41:14Z","email":"chifor@gmail.com","name":"Constantin Chifor"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-11T00:41:14Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(ci): add Node and Rust project CI workflows (#229)\n\nGenerated Node and Rust projects shipped no CI workflow — only\n`_common/ci_python.yml` existed, so `_ci_source_for` returned None for\nevery non-Python backend and multi-backend projects got only the first\nbackend''s `ci.yml`.\n\nAdd `_common/ci_node.yml` (npm install, prisma generate, biome lint,\ntsc build, vitest, npm audit) and `_common/ci_rust.yml` (rustfmt\n--check, clippy, cargo build/test, cargo-audit), mirroring the\nPython workflow''s posture (no DB service; lint + build + test).\nRust uses runtime-checked sqlx, so `cargo build` needs no database.\n\n`apply_common_files` now emits one workflow per distinct backend\nlanguage: the first keeps the canonical `ci.yml` name (back-compat,\ngolden-stable for single-backend projects); each additional language\ngets `ci-<lang>.yml`. Tests cover node-only, rust-only, multi-backend\nper-language emission, and duplicate-language collapse; node/rust/multi\ngoldens regenerated.\n\nLockfile generation + Docker `npm ci`/`--locked` + digest pins remain\na follow-up (need real toolchains at generation time). Refs #223.","tree":{"sha":"75fd5b39785112b13542223a37a5835171d79bb3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge/git/trees/75fd5b39785112b13542223a37a5835171d79bb3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cchifor/forge